WEBVTT

00:00.050 --> 00:06.303
AI agents are moving from conversation into real execution.

00:06.303 --> 00:11.750
They call APIs, update systems, and can move money.

00:11.750 --> 00:19.625
But a decision that was valid when planned may no longer be valid when execution begins.

00:19.625 --> 00:27.660
And an API accepting a request does not prove the intended outcome actually happened.

00:27.660 --> 00:31.125
Traditional automation trusts a plan.

00:31.125 --> 00:41.821
Autonomous agents need a stronger contract: permission must still be true when an action crosses the execution boundary.

00:41.821 --> 00:48.839
AgentProof separates probabilistic planning from deterministic execution truth.

00:48.839 --> 00:55.375
We use Gemini 3.6 Flash with Google A D K.

00:55.375 --> 00:58.392
Gemini decides what to do.

00:58.392 --> 01:02.517
AgentProof determines what actually happened.

01:02.517 --> 01:10.875
Gemini can select a constrained scenario, but it cannot emit or change the final proof.

01:10.875 --> 01:20.267
In the normal path, Gemini receives a natural-language goal and invokes the AgentProof payment tool.

01:20.267 --> 01:31.660
The authorization is fresh, the action matches the grant, the simulated payment settles, and the ledger proves the state transition.

01:31.660 --> 01:39.642
The grant binds the invoice, vendor, amount, and execution key before dispatch.

01:39.642 --> 01:44.339
Only then does AgentProof issue VERIFIED.

01:44.339 --> 01:47.053
Now the dangerous case.

01:47.053 --> 01:54.285
The payment is authorized, but before execution the vendor policy changes.

01:54.285 --> 01:58.339
The agent had permission when it planned the payment.

01:58.339 --> 02:02.500
It did not have permission when execution began.

02:02.500 --> 02:09.714
AgentProof revalidates authority at the dispatch boundary and blocks the action.

02:09.714 --> 02:12.232
Zero dollars move.

02:12.232 --> 02:18.785
The epoch mismatch is evidence, not an exception the system ignores.

02:18.785 --> 02:26.267
Next, the provider accepts the request, but no settlement appears in the ledger.

02:26.267 --> 02:30.464
AgentProof returns UNVERIFIED.

02:30.464 --> 02:33.339
Accepted is not settled.

02:33.339 --> 02:36.071
Dispatch is not outcome.

02:36.071 --> 02:40.125
Finally, the same execution is replayed.

02:40.125 --> 02:46.821
AgentProof detects the existing execution key and returns DUPLICATE.

02:46.821 --> 02:50.089
No second payment is created.

02:50.089 --> 02:59.821
This system runs on Google Cloud Run and uses Gemini 3.6 Flash through Vertex A I.

02:59.821 --> 03:17.553
The project is reproducibly tested in GitHub Actions, with ten regression tests covering authorization freshness, outcome grounding, replay safety, concurrency, and deterministic verdict authority.

03:17.553 --> 03:24.732
The model can propose a tool call, but it cannot rewrite AgentProof's receipt.

03:24.732 --> 03:32.553
Every receipt has a canonical SHA-256 digest for audit.

03:32.553 --> 03:37.071
AI agents should be free to act autonomously.

03:37.071 --> 03:42.142
But autonomy without verification is just trust.

03:42.142 --> 03:46.803
AgentProof turns agent actions into evidence.

03:46.803 --> 03:50.660
Don't trust what an AI agent says it did.

03:50.660 --> 03:53.017
Prove what actually happened.
